license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  An observatory of how the W3C/OGC Semantic Sensor Network ontology (SSN) and its core,
  SOSA, are used in the scientific literature: every work that cites a publication on
  SOSA/SSN or writes its names in its full text, with how it uses SOSA/SSN (engagement,
  version, modules, terms, results and values, errors, domain, companion vocabularies,
  published artefacts, reported gaps, modelling patterns), coded by language models, agents
  and scripts; a knowledge graph (FaBiO, CiTO, MOD, PROV-O) and a static web application to
  browse and query it. Data under CC BY 4.0, code under MIT. No full text is included.
keywords:
  - SOSA
  - SSN
  - Semantic Sensor Network ontology
  - ontology usage
  - knowledge graph
  - scholarly knowledge graph
  - systematic mapping
  - W3C
  - OGC
  - Linked Data
# preferred-citation: the ESWC 2027 resource paper, once accepted
